15
00:00:47,890 --> 00:00:50,190
Let's get started with the first part.

16
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:57,200
Sentence completion is a question type in which

17
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:01,060
some incomplete sentences are provided and candidates are

18
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:03,720
required to fill in the blanks with exact

19
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:05,540
words taken from the reading passage.

20
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:09,000
This question type is not too challenging but

21
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,160
we still need to stay focused to find

22
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:14,280
the suitable information to fill in the blanks.

23
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:16,900
In the previous lesson, you learned the steps

24
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:18,980
for completion questions in IELTS reading.

25
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:22,680
So, let's do the interactive question below to

26
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:23,960
see if you remember them.

27
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:28,060
Do you remember all the steps?

28
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:30,400
We're going to apply them to handle the

29
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,480
reading passage below.

30
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:44,840
Let's start with the first step.

31
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:46,080
Step 1.

32
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:49,520
Read the question's requirement carefully.

33
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:52,620
Reading the question's requirement will provide us with

34
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:54,720
the following two pieces of information.

35
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:56,920
Type of completion question.

36
00:01:57,580 --> 00:01:59,140
Word limit for each blank.

37
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:03,040
With this requirement, what information can we have?

38
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:24,120
The requirement has the phrase "Complete the sentences below"

39
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:28,280
So, this is the sentence completion question type.

40
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:32,520
Furthermore, we are required to choose no more

41
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:35,940
than two words which means we are not

42
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:40,380
allowed to write more than two words for each blank.

43
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:46,020
After understanding the question's requirement, we'll move to...

44
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:49,320
Read each question carefully and predict the answer.

45
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:53,020
As stated in the previous lessons, every time

46
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:55,040
you handle a question, you should read it

47
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:57,080
carefully to use prediction skill.

48
00:02:57,560 --> 00:03:00,600
Predict about the answer you need to write.

49
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:04,120
Prediction skill is very important in completion questions

50
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:07,560
because making detailed predictions will help us find

51
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:10,220
the information faster and more correctly.

52
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:13,740
Here are some aspects to consider when you

53
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:15,580
make predictions about the answer.

54
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:18,380
Grammar and word form.

55
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:22,820
Does the blank need a noun, verb, adjective

56
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:24,660
or any other word form?

57
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:29,420
If the answer is a noun, is it a singular or plural noun?

58
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:33,200
If it is a verb, is it to verb?

59
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:38,300
Verb ending with ing or verb infinitive?

60
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:39,600
Content.

61
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:44,700
If it is a noun, is it a noun referring to a person?

62
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:47,720
Or a noun referring to an object?

63
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:50,800
Or a noun referring to an event?

64
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:54,520
If it is an adjective, is it an

65
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:57,920
adjective describing personalities or objects?

66
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:01,780
Now, let's apply our prediction skills to the

67
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:04,760
first three questions of our passage.

68
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:08,680
Homeschooling – Learning Beyond the Classroom.

69
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:13,560
Remember, making detailed predictions helps us find the

70
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:16,500
information faster and more accurately.

71
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:17,820
Question one.

72
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:20,980
Homeschooling allows children to study 

73
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:24,220
without attending a .... school.

74
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:27,000
For grammar and word form, we are looking

75
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,940
for an adjective because the blank is placed

76
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:32,680
directly before the noun school.

77
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:36,280
As for content, the answer will likely be

78
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:39,380
a word that describes a type or category

79
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:42,360
of school that is different from homeschooling.

80
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:44,020
Question two.

81
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:48,100
Homeschooled students can choose the most suitable ...

82
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:51,160
For grammar and word form, the blank follows

83
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:54,540
the adjective suitable, so we need a noun.

84
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:58,720
It could be a singular, plural or uncountable noun.

85
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:02,040
For content, the answer should refer to something

86
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:05,140
that can be chosen or customized in a

87
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:06,960
homeschooling environment.

88
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:11,560
For example, a time, a place or a program.

89
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:15,980
For question three, students become more confident and

90
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:18,620
stay ... through personalized learning.

91
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:21,740
For grammar and word form, the blank follows

92
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:25,160
the linking verb stay and is connected by

93
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:27,540
the conjunction and to confident.

94
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:31,440
Therefore, we need an adjective that is parallel

95
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:33,880
in meaning to confident.

96
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:37,320
The answer will be a word describing a

97
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:41,940
positive mental state or feeling a student has while learning.

98
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:46,080
Now it's your turn to apply this prediction skill 

99
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:48,140
to the remaining questions.

100
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:53,740
With step three, apply scanning skills to locate information.

101
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,860
In the previous lessons, we learned three steps

102
00:05:56,860 --> 00:05:57,720
for scanning.

103
00:05:58,520 --> 00:05:59,140
Number one.

104
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:02,020
Identify keywords in questions.

105
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,080
We have two main types of keywords.

106
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:07,520
Unchangeable keywords.

107
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:13,060
Proper nouns, acronyms, numbers, scientific or academic terms.

108
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,400
Changeable keywords.

109
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:19,480
Nouns, verbs, adjectives, adverbs.

110
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,740
Because they are often keywords 

111
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:23,980
carrying the main content of the sentence.

112
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:27,680
Let's identify keywords in sentence one.

113
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:30,373
Homeschooling allows children to study 

114
00:06:30,370 --> 00:06:33,376
without attending a ... school.

115
00:06:33,780 --> 00:06:37,040
Homeschooling is a changeable keyword noun.

116
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:40,580
but since it's the main topic of the text,

117
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:43,260
it will appear everywhere in the passage.

118
00:06:43,260 --> 00:06:45,140
Attending and school.

119
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:48,040
These are changeable keywords.

120
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:53,040
Without, this is a crucial logic keyword that

121
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:56,820
shows a negative relationship not doing something.

122
00:06:57,840 --> 00:07:02,040
Next step for scanning is identify scanning words

123
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,160
among keywords.

124
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:05,040
Unchangeable keywords.

125
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:06,200
Compounds.

126
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:07,700
Long words.

127
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:12,300
In this sentence, attending and school are our

128
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:13,980
best scanning words.

129
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:17,820
While homeschooling is the title, we need to

130
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:21,100
find the specific part of the text that

131
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:25,060
mentions not going to a certain type of school.

132
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:28,840
Next, we need to find keywords or synonyms

133
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,920
in the passage.

134
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:33,620
Tip one, look for the scanning words first.

135
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:36,720
Tip two, be ready for synonyms.

136
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:40,160
When we scan the first paragraph, we find

137
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:43,620
homeschooling is a way of learning where children

138
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:47,100
study at home instead of going to a traditional school.

139
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:50,740
The phrase without attending in the question is

140
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:54,820
a synonym for instead of going to in the text.

141
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:57,920
The word school matches perfectly.

142
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:02,300
This narrows our focus to just this one sentence.

143
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:04,920
Now we can move to the final step.

144
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:09,520
Now please read that sentence carefully and do step four.

145
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:12,380
Find and fill in the answer.

146
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:15,478
Based on the predictions in step two,

147
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:18,140
we will find the correct answer from the sentence

148
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:20,880
we've just scanned and then write it on

149
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:23,486
the answer sheet if you take the paper-based test 

150
00:08:23,490 --> 00:08:26,760
or copy and paste the answer directly onto the blanks

151
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:28,900
if you take the computer-based test.

152
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:32,580
Based on our previous prediction, we needed an

153
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:34,740
adjective to describe the school.

154
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:37,520
We look at the word right before the

155
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:39,799
word school in the text.

156
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:42,400
We select the word traditional.

157
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,200
If you are on a computer-based test,

158
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,860
you can copy-paste it.

159
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:51,240
If on paper, write it clearly on your answer sheet.

160
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:55,080
After step four, to be more careful, you

161
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:58,080
should do an additional step which is to check the answer.

162
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:00,820
You should check whether the word or phrase

163
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:02,880
you filled in meets the following criteria.

164
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:05,420
Does it satisfy the word limit?

165
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:08,560
Does it match the word form and grammar?

166
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:11,600
Does it match the meaning of the sentence?

